Different methods of scale setting result in different parameter estimates and different standard errors (for details you can see: https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1037/1082-989X.6.3.258). Given that the simple slopes (and their standard errors) are functions of the model parameters it makes sense that these would be different.

